.MARINE...
(Today through Thursday)
Issued at 919 AM PST Sat Nov 21 2026

A cold front will bring rain this afternoon into the evening and
overnight hours with southerly breezes ahead of it and
northwesterly breezes behind it. Another round of rainfall is
expected Sunday morning into the afternoon with the most impactful
system likely Tuesday into Wednesday. Moderate to rough seas will
prevail through Monday with hazardous conditions across the
northern outer waters Sunday and Monday for 10 foot seas. Strong
to near gale southerly breezes will spread from north to south
across the waters Monday into Tuesday. Seas will build to become
rough to very rough as a result.

