.BEACHES...
Issued at 1214 PM PST Sat Nov 21 2026

Coastal flooding will be a major impact this week. The combination
of king tides, storm surge, and thermal expansion from warm El
Nino waters will bring the tide to near record territory. A
Coastal Flood Advisory in effect for the San Francisco Bay until 6
AM PST Monday, at which point it will be upgraded to a Coastal
Flood Warning through Thursday. A Coastal Flood Advisory is also in
effect for the Pacific Coast through Thursday. At the San
Francisco tide gauge, high tide is expected to be 2.0 ft above
normal (7.8 ft MLLW) at 8:48 AM Sunday, 2.2 ft above normal (8.0
ft MLLW) at 9:25 AM Monday, 2.6 ft above normal (8.4 ft MLLW) at
10:05 AM Tuesday, 2.8 ft above normal (8.6 ft MLLW) at 10:49 AM
Wednesday, and 2.4 ft above normal (8.2 ft MLLW) at 11:38 AM
Thursday. These predictions include up to 1.6 ft of surge that
will enhance the astronomical tide and flooding threat. High tide
varies up to 90 minutes earlier or later along the Pacific Coast
and through the San Francisco Bay, respectively.

